                "content": "# SACRAMENTO RIVER BASIN\n\n# SACRAMENTO RIVER BELOW WILKINS SLOUGH, CALIF.\n\nLOCATION.-Water-stage recorder in Jimeno land grant, Colusa County, 1,500 feet below Wilkins Slough and 6 miles southeast of Grimes. (Location formerly published in error.)\n\nRECORDS AVAILABLE. - August 1931 to October 1932 (low-water records only). EXTREMES.-Minimum discharge during summer 1932, 895 second-feet Aug. 11. 1931-32: Minimum discharge, 100 second-feet Aug. 1, 1931.\n\n- REMARKS.-Records good. Storage, regulation, and many diversions above\nstation.\n\nDischarge, in second-feet, 1931-32",
